{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>This is the law of the animal and the fowl and every living creature that swarms in the water.</b> Scripture placed the fowl between the animal and the swarming creature of the water. To exempt it entirely is impossible, for it has already been compared to the animal, to obligate it in two signs. To obligate it in two is impossible, for it has already been compared to fish. How then? Its fitness is by one sign." "<b>And to every swarming creature.</b> To some, it is superfluous, like לכל כליו תעשה נחשת ('all its vessels you shall make of copper')."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:34.478292108Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}